"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"helminthiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.97,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"itch_scabies","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"jaundice","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.98,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"joint_pain","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.9,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"liver_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.88,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"pain","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.78,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"plague","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.96,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"poisoning","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.96,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"rabies","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"scrofula","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"urolithiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:136-gentian-felwort-or-baldmony":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Gentian, Felwort, Or Baldmony","headword":"Gentian, Felwort, Or Baldmony","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"They are under the dominion of Mars, and one of the principal herbs he is ruler of. They resist putrefactions, poison, and a more sure remedy cannot be found to prevent the pestilence than it is; it strengthens the stomach exceedingly, helps digestion, comforts the heart, and preserves it against faintings and swoonings: The powder of the dry roots helps the biting of mad dogs and venomous beasts, opens obstructions of the liver, and restores an appetite for their meat to such as have lost it. The herb steeped in wine, and the wine drank, refreshes such as be over-weary with traveling, and grow lame in their joints, either by cold or evil lodgings; it helps stitches, and griping pains in the sides; is an excellent remedy for such as are bruised by falls; it provokes urine and the terms exceedingly, therefore let it not be given to women with child: The same is very profitable for such as are troubled with cramps and convulsions, to drink the decoction: Also they say it breaks the stone, and helps ruptures most certainly: it is excellent in all cold diseases, and such as are troubled with tough phlegm, scabs, itch, or any fretting sores and ulcers; it is an admirable remedy to kill the worms, by taking half a dram of the powder in a morning in any convenient liquor; the same is excellently good to be taken inwardly for the king’s evil. It helps agues of all sorts, and the yellow jaundice, as also the bots in cattle; when kine are bitten on the udder by any venomous beast, do but stroke the place with the decoction of any of these, and it will instantly heal them.","spans":[{"start":111,"end":117,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":173,"end":183,"concept_id":"plague","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":199,"end":222,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":242,"end":251,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":253,"end":271,"concept_id":"heart","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":298,"end":307,"concept_id":"heart","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":312,"end":321,"concept_id":"heart","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":371,"end":379,"concept_id":"rabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":384,"end":392,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":401,"end":432,"concept_id":"liver_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":450,"end":458,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":602,"end":622,"concept_id":"joint_pain","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":666,"end":674,"concept_id":"pain","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":680,"end":687,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":747,"end":763,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":768,"end":796,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":820,"end":859,"concept_id":"abortifacient","polarity":"adverse"},{"start":919,"end":925,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":930,"end":941,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":995,"end":1000,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1119,"end":1124,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1126,"end":1130,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1148,"end":1153,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1158,"end":1164,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1204,"end":1209,"concept_id":"helminthiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1344,"end":1355,"concept_id":"scrofula","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1366,"end":1371,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1401,"end":1409,"concept_id":"jaundice","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1453,"end":1459,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1480,"end":1488,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:136-gentian-felwort-or-baldmony":{"111":"resists / expels poison","173":"pestilence, pestilential fevers / sores","199":"strengthens / comforts the stomach (stomachic)","242":"digestion / indigestion","253":"comforts / strengthens / defends the heart","298":"faintings, fainting spirits","312":"swoonings: syncope","371":"biting of a mad dog: rabies","384":"venomous beasts / creatures","401":"opens obstructions of / strengthens the liver","450":"appetite (provokes / restores)","602":"joints full of pain / stiff; lame in their joints","666":"stitch: sharp pain in the side","680":"gripings: colicky abdominal pains","747":"bruised inwardly / by falls","768":"provokes / brings down the terms, courses: emmenagogue","820":"not to be given to women with child","919":"cramp, cramps","930":"convulsions","995":"the stone (urinary calculus)","1119":"scabs: scabies / scabby skin","1126":"itch, itches, itching","1148":"sores, running sores","1158":"ulcers (old, foul, running, fretting)","1204":"worms (intestinal)","1344":"king's evil: scrofula","1366":"agues: intermittent fevers","1401":"yellow jaundice, black jaundice","1453":"bitten or stung","1480":"venomous beasts / creatures"}},"images":[]}